SUMMARY:Karnataka High Court: A writ petition by four petitioners to quash 
 the FIR the Suddaguntepalya police in Bengaluru registered on 7 October ov
 er Form 7 applications filed to delete six electors\, which concerns alleg
 ations against the Jayanagar MLA of the BJP\, C K Ramamurthy\, and three o
 thers\, W.P. No. 32768 of 2026
DESCRIPTION:A writ petition by four petitioners to quash the FIR the Suddag
 untepalya police in Bengaluru registered on 7 October over Form 7 applicat
 ions filed to delete six electors\, which concerns allegations against the
  Jayanagar MLA of the BJP\, C K Ramamurthy\, and three others\, W.P. No. 3
 2768 of 2026. The petition is next listed on this date. On 20 November the
  Court declined to stay the investigation\, directed that the petitioners 
 not be arrested and that no chargesheet be filed without its leave\, issue
 d notice to the complainant and asked the petitioners to serve the petitio
 n on the Election Commission's standing counsel. Court: Karnataka High Cou
 rt. Source: LawChakra\, https://lawchakra.in/high-court/karnataka-high-cou
 rt/form-7-voter-deletion/ More: https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/#d-fo
 rm7-99
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://offtheroll.in/india/disputes/
